Actually it's around 22.5% (3/13 if on the "good" path, 3/25 if on the
bad path), leaving the total at around 1.4% for every container you
open with zero luck. Also, you have to get up to +4 or +5 luck before
electric traps become less likely, because the added chance of
a dud is (more than) outweighed by the additional chance of a
non-dud being electric. All calculations per wikihack. (Actually
wikihack is a little ambiguous here; it might be 3/14 and 3/26,
which would knock the percentage down to 20.8%.)

That's definitely a small enough chance that you can open
containers willy-nilly without getting most of your games
wrecked -- that's what I do. (And even when my wizards
did get their scrolls burnt, there were other scrolls along
later, though losing the AC was kind of annoying.) Depends
on play style, I suppose.


